  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) has been completed, yielding 48.5% accuracy / 46.4% F1 — a very weak baseline with no information about whether the image modality, better encoders, or multiprofile aggregation contribute. Question being tested: Does adding the image modality (resnet50, concat fusion) to the existing RNA baseline improve performance? This is the most fundamental design question for a multimodal cellular profiling study. Why this is the best next experiment: config_016 is the minimal, cleanest extension of config_001 — same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), same profile setting (singleprofile), simply adding resnet50 image features with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of modality addition with minimal confounds. If multimodal outperforms the RNA-only baseline, it validates the multimodal direction and justifies subsequent investment in better encoders/fusion. If it does not, it signals that the bottleneck lies in representation quality (RNA or image encoder) rather than modality combination, redirecting the search efficiently. Under a tight budget, resolving this binary question is more informative than, e.g., testing a different RNA encoder in isolation, because it determines the entire architecture of subsequent experiments."
}

